WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.091 --> 00:00:01.487
- All we are back.

00:00:01.487 --> 00:00:03.020
And you may remember earlier this season

00:00:03.020 --> 00:00:05.070
we welcomed the cast of "Black Adam,"

00:00:05.070 --> 00:00:08.386
Dwayne Johnson, Noah
Centineo, Aldis Hodge,

00:00:08.386 --> 00:00:10.440
Quintessa Swindell, and Pierce Brosnan,

00:00:10.440 --> 00:00:11.610
amazing group of actors.

00:00:11.610 --> 00:00:13.560
It was fun show and we
had a lot to chat about

00:00:13.560 --> 00:00:16.260
and it all couldn't fit
into our original episode.

00:00:16.260 --> 00:00:17.430
In fact, we actually did a round

00:00:17.430 --> 00:00:19.380
of the ultimate Twitter
questionnaire during which

00:00:19.380 --> 00:00:22.170
they answered some pretty
interesting fan questions.

00:00:22.170 --> 00:00:25.470
We didn't want you to miss
any of it, so check this out.

00:00:25.470 --> 00:00:26.320
Okay, here we go.

00:00:28.832 --> 00:00:29.665
(bell dings)
Okay.

00:00:29.665 --> 00:00:30.498
Oh, this is for Aldis.

00:00:30.498 --> 00:00:32.910
So rumor has it that The Rock called you

00:00:32.910 --> 00:00:34.230
to tell you that you got the role.

00:00:34.230 --> 00:00:35.520
Is is there any truth to that?

00:00:35.520 --> 00:00:38.465
Wait, what's that smirk?
- Because, true story.

00:00:38.465 --> 00:00:39.298
- It is?

00:00:39.298 --> 00:00:40.200
- [Noah] Why don't you
tell them I just Aldis?

00:00:40.200 --> 00:00:41.250
- DJ.
- Yes.

00:00:41.250 --> 00:00:43.183
- Would you like to navigate this story?

00:00:43.183 --> 00:00:44.490
- I'll set it up.

00:00:44.490 --> 00:00:46.140
So he-
- I dunno, he's the best.

00:00:47.011 --> 00:00:49.290
- Aldis sends in his tape.

00:00:49.290 --> 00:00:52.378
He was good enough to send in his tape.

00:00:52.378 --> 00:00:54.630
And we all watched it.

00:00:54.630 --> 00:00:56.940
I watched it, loved it.

00:00:56.940 --> 00:00:58.200
I called up our producers

00:00:58.200 --> 00:01:00.090
and Jaume Collet-Serra, our director.

00:01:00.090 --> 00:01:01.590
I said, I really think that's our guy.

00:01:01.590 --> 00:01:03.120
That should be Hawkman.

00:01:03.120 --> 00:01:04.530
And then everyone agreed.

00:01:04.530 --> 00:01:07.170
And then, so I said, "You
know, let me call him up."

00:01:07.170 --> 00:01:08.220
I've never talked to him before.

00:01:08.220 --> 00:01:09.097
Let me just call him up and say,

00:01:09.097 --> 00:01:10.890
"Hey brother, welcome to 'Black Adam.'"

00:01:10.890 --> 00:01:11.910
That was my intention.

00:01:11.910 --> 00:01:14.557
So I call him and I say, "Hey, is Aldis-"

00:01:14.557 --> 00:01:16.080
"Hello, is Aldi there?"

00:01:16.080 --> 00:01:17.380
And he goes, "Who's this?"

00:01:18.390 --> 00:01:20.130
Right away the energy, fun.

00:01:20.130 --> 00:01:21.870
Like, "who's this," attitude.

00:01:21.870 --> 00:01:25.050
I went, "Hey, this is Dwayne Johnson."

00:01:25.050 --> 00:01:28.251
And the following curse words-

00:01:28.251 --> 00:01:29.280
(Aldis laughs)

00:01:29.280 --> 00:01:31.950
That came out as if it wasn't me.

00:01:31.950 --> 00:01:33.300
So then I'll let him take the story.

00:01:33.300 --> 00:01:34.133
- So check it out.

00:01:34.133 --> 00:01:37.217
Somebody happened had been
crank calling my phone.

00:01:37.217 --> 00:01:40.410
Anytime somebody calls
from a random number,

00:01:40.410 --> 00:01:42.600
and says, "Hey, is Aldis Hodge there?"

00:01:42.600 --> 00:01:44.433
It's either a bill collector,

00:01:45.390 --> 00:01:47.280
somebody trying to get my-

00:01:47.280 --> 00:01:48.750
who I'm voting for,

00:01:48.750 --> 00:01:50.190
or somebody playing with my phone.

00:01:50.190 --> 00:01:53.220
So I said, "Look man,
stop playing on my phone.

00:01:53.220 --> 00:01:54.870
I don't have time for this today."

00:01:54.870 --> 00:01:55.830
We got kids watching

00:01:55.830 --> 00:01:58.200
so we ain't gonna get
into the particulars.

00:01:58.200 --> 00:01:59.287
I said, "Bro, stop playing on."

00:01:59.287 --> 00:02:01.530
"No, it's Dwayne Johnson," da, da, da.

00:02:01.530 --> 00:02:03.270
You know, he's being real cool, chill.

00:02:03.270 --> 00:02:05.250
I said, "Bro, I'm serious.

00:02:05.250 --> 00:02:06.660
Don't play with my emotions."

00:02:06.660 --> 00:02:08.853
Day after my birthday, I'm in quarantine.

00:02:10.376 --> 00:02:12.210
- I'm feeling crazy.
- I don't have time

00:02:12.210 --> 00:02:13.530
for this emotional rollercoaster.

00:02:13.530 --> 00:02:15.067
But then he goes into,

00:02:15.067 --> 00:02:18.030
"Hey look," da da dah,
"Welcome to 'Black Adam."

00:02:18.030 --> 00:02:19.620
Well, actually he
started telling me about,

00:02:19.620 --> 00:02:21.097
you know, the tape and all that,

00:02:21.097 --> 00:02:22.260
"Saw your tape, loved it."

00:02:22.260 --> 00:02:24.570
I thought he was calling to
tell me I didn't get the job.

00:02:24.570 --> 00:02:25.590
And you know, boom.

00:02:25.590 --> 00:02:27.210
But then he says,
"Welcome to 'Black Adam.'"

00:02:27.210 --> 00:02:28.890
And I had a moment where I said, oh.

00:02:28.890 --> 00:02:31.260
I legit almost hung up on this man.

00:02:31.260 --> 00:02:32.460
Lost the job of my life.

00:02:33.750 --> 00:02:34.980
So I appreciate your patience,

00:02:34.980 --> 00:02:36.263
you know what I'm saying?
- Yes.

00:02:37.406 --> 00:02:38.438
(audience applauds)

00:02:38.438 --> 00:02:42.360
- At the same time,
you're not expecting call.

00:02:42.360 --> 00:02:44.280
- Who expects a call from The Rock?

00:02:44.280 --> 00:02:45.993
Like, you know what I'm saying?

00:02:45.993 --> 00:02:46.826
It's outta the blue .

00:02:46.826 --> 00:02:47.868
"Hey man, it's Dwayne Johnson."

00:02:47.868 --> 00:02:50.332
I'm like, you are doing a really
good impression right now.

00:02:50.332 --> 00:02:52.272
- Oh, my god.
- This is not okay.

00:02:52.272 --> 00:02:53.105
- True.

00:02:53.105 --> 00:02:54.450
- Sometimes you gotta be careful
when you answer the phone.

00:02:54.450 --> 00:02:58.376
But I answered my phone and
Robert also does Stevie Nicks.

00:02:58.376 --> 00:02:59.610
My hair guy.

00:02:59.610 --> 00:03:02.910
And I was inebriated and I answered.

00:03:02.910 --> 00:03:04.740
And I thought it'd be
funny to answer with Robert

00:03:04.740 --> 00:03:06.420
and be like, "What's up?"

00:03:06.420 --> 00:03:10.935
And Stevie Nicks was on the
phone and I was like, "Hello."

00:03:10.935 --> 00:03:11.768
"Hello."

00:03:11.768 --> 00:03:14.970
I was trying to like not be inebriated.

00:03:14.970 --> 00:03:16.027
And then I called him back and I was like,

00:03:16.027 --> 00:03:19.050
"You can't just call
someone's number like that."

00:03:19.050 --> 00:03:20.250
- Oh, my gosh.

00:03:20.250 --> 00:03:21.300
He gave me the tequila.

00:03:21.300 --> 00:03:22.133
I blame him.
- Your like, sorry.

00:03:22.133 --> 00:03:23.250
I usually sip my tequila...

00:03:23.250 --> 00:03:26.520
- Yeah, I was trying
to be so cool about it.

00:03:26.520 --> 00:03:27.870
And then by the time I
got off the phone call,

00:03:27.870 --> 00:03:29.370
I was like, she's so rock and roll.

00:03:29.370 --> 00:03:30.750
Why am I being weird about it?

00:03:30.750 --> 00:03:32.580
Anyway, we can edit that out.

00:03:32.580 --> 00:03:33.930
There's nothing to do with anything.

00:03:33.930 --> 00:03:35.160
Okay, we got one more.

00:03:35.160 --> 00:03:35.993
One more.

00:03:38.333 --> 00:03:39.810
Oh, for Quintessa.

00:03:39.810 --> 00:03:41.347
With the greatest name ever.

00:03:41.347 --> 00:03:44.758
"So who do you want Cyclone
to work with in the future?"

00:03:44.758 --> 00:03:45.787
#BlackAdam.

00:03:45.787 --> 00:03:46.863
#BlackAdam.

00:03:47.976 --> 00:03:49.710
- Hmm.
- Oh, interesting.

00:03:49.710 --> 00:03:52.053
- I don't know, I don't know.

00:03:54.660 --> 00:03:58.380
It'd be really cool to
work with or see Cyclone

00:03:58.380 --> 00:04:02.193
in juxtaposition to like maybe Harlequin.

00:04:03.600 --> 00:04:05.040
- Nice.
- That could be fun.

00:04:05.040 --> 00:04:06.990
- Yeah.
- That could be interesting.

00:04:06.990 --> 00:04:08.430
- Write that.
- Well I love that.

00:04:08.430 --> 00:04:09.930
Well, the cool thing about our world

00:04:09.930 --> 00:04:12.180
that we've all created
here about "Black Adam"

00:04:12.180 --> 00:04:14.310
and this universe of JSA is

00:04:14.310 --> 00:04:18.610
we believe that all the
characters in the DC universe

00:04:19.710 --> 00:04:21.570
can mix and intermingle.

00:04:21.570 --> 00:04:23.620
So we should work on that right now.

00:04:23.620 --> 00:04:25.350
- I love that.

00:04:25.350 --> 00:04:27.660
And that only gets fans excited.

00:04:27.660 --> 00:04:28.920
We love that.

00:04:28.920 --> 00:04:30.360
We're just like, "Oh, my god."

00:04:30.360 --> 00:04:31.530
- Yeah.
- That's so cool.

00:04:31.530 --> 00:04:33.180
Great idea.

00:04:33.180 --> 00:04:36.330
Okay, so Pierce, this
one's not in the computer,

00:04:36.330 --> 00:04:40.833
but what is Dr. Fate's
favorite Pierce Brosnan movie?

00:04:43.680 --> 00:04:45.000
Please say "Thomas Crown Affair."

00:04:45.000 --> 00:04:47.160
Just makes sense that Dr.
Fate would like that one.

00:04:47.160 --> 00:04:47.993
- Ba-boom.

00:04:47.993 --> 00:04:49.260
Said it without moving my lips.

00:04:49.260 --> 00:04:50.400
There you go.

00:04:50.400 --> 00:04:52.657
- Now what would you
say, what would you say?

00:04:52.657 --> 00:04:54.090
- "Thomas Crown" is a great movie.

00:04:54.090 --> 00:04:55.170
I'm very proud of that film.

00:04:55.170 --> 00:04:57.060
- Well, I just mean how trippy it is.

00:04:57.060 --> 00:04:58.470
Like, how it tricks, you know?

00:04:58.470 --> 00:05:02.610
Like that whole scene in the
museum, it's very Dr. Fate.

00:05:02.610 --> 00:05:03.780
- It is very Dr. Fate.

00:05:03.780 --> 00:05:05.989
- I sound like a stalker?

00:05:05.989 --> 00:05:08.280
(Pierce laughs)

00:05:08.280 --> 00:05:09.113
- No, it's a good movie.

00:05:09.113 --> 00:05:10.380
And that would be a good choice.

00:05:10.380 --> 00:05:11.250
Yes.

00:05:11.250 --> 00:05:13.750
- Next time I'm gonna let
you answer the question.

00:05:14.820 --> 00:05:16.847
- Well, you're so enthusiastic.

00:05:16.847 --> 00:05:18.597
It is your show.

00:05:18.597 --> 00:05:19.950
- I'm like, wouldn't it have been nice?

00:05:19.950 --> 00:05:20.783
My producer's gonna be like,

00:05:20.783 --> 00:05:23.460
so maybe next time let them answer it.

00:05:23.460 --> 00:05:24.483
Cool, duly noted.

